 name: "Publish Release to Maven Repository"
+# Deploys a Gradle release to the e-CODEX JFrog Artifactory (scm.ecodex.eu) with the JFrog CLI.
+#
+# What is done and why:
+#   - Authentication: GitHub OIDC token exchanged by the JFrog CLI for a short-lived JFrog token (no secrets).
+#   - Deployment: 'jf gradle artifactoryPublish' deploys every Gradle publication (jars, POMs, distribution zip)
+#     and records them, with all resolved dependencies, in the JFrog build-info '<repository>'. The build-info is
+#     what Artifactory (and Xray) use to know where an artifact comes from and what it contains.
+#   - SBOM: the CycloneDX 'cyclonedxBom' task produces the aggregated SBOM of the project; it is deployed next to
+#     the distribution zip as '<zip name>-cyclonedx.json' so consumers find it beside the artifact they download.
+#   - Attestations: the distribution zip (the artifact users actually install) gets a SLSA build-provenance
+#     attestation and an SBOM attestation, signed with Sigstore and stored in GitHub. Their subject is the zip's
+#     path in Artifactory, so the setup-jfrog-cli post step can attach them to the zip as JFrog evidence.
+#   - End of job (setup-jfrog-cli post step): adds the git details, publishes the build-info and creates the
+#     JFrog evidence from the attestations.
 on:
     workflow_call:
         inputs:
@@ -13,9 +27,24 @@ on:
                 type: string
                 default: ""
             maven-repo-id:
-                description: "Maven repository ID"
+                description: "Deprecated and ignored: the JFrog CLI deploys to 'deploy-repo'"
+                required: false
+                type: string
